-- title:
--   Local integrability of a shifted Godement–Jacquet zeta integrand
-- statement:
--   Fix a height-one prime $p$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$, a character $\theta_0 : (\mathbb{Q}_p)^\times \to \mathbb{C}^\times$, and a nonzero ideal $N$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$, and let $w_2^{\mathrm{base}} : \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_p) \to \mathbb{C}$ satisfy: the Whittaker transformation law $w_2^{\mathrm{base}}(u(x)g) = \psi_p(x)\, w_2^{\mathrm{base}}(g)$ for all $x \in \mathbb{Q}_p$ and $g$, where $u(x) = \begin{pmatrix}1&x\\0&1\end{pmatrix}$ and $\psi_p$ is `psiLocal`, the local additive character obtained by composing the standard adelic character of $\mathbb{Q}$ with the additive inclusion of $\mathbb{Q}_p$ at $p$; right invariance under `localLevelOne` at level $N$, the preimage in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_p)$, under the embedding at $p$ into $\mathrm{GL}_2$ of the finite adeles, of the group of $g$ with both $g$ and $g^{-1}$ level-one matrices for $N$; non-vanishing $w_2^{\mathrm{base}} \neq 0$; the cyclicity condition that every nonzero element $w$ of the $\mathbb{C}$-span $V$ of the right translates $g \mapsto w_2^{\mathrm{base}}(gh)$ has $w_2^{\mathrm{base}}$ in the span of its own right translates; admissibility, namely for each open subgroup $U \le \mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_p)$ a finite set $B$ of functions whose span contains every right $U$-invariant member of $V$; and the central character law $w_2^{\mathrm{base}}(zI\cdot g) = \theta_0(z)\, w_2^{\mathrm{base}}(g)$. Let $\chi : (\mathbb{Q}_p)^\times \to \mathbb{C}^\times$ be a locally constant character. Then, with $\mathbb{Q}_p$ and $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_p)$ carrying their Borel structures, for every Haar measure $\mu_2$ on $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{Q}_p)$, every $w \in V$, every locally constant compactly supported $\Phi : M_2(\mathbb{Q}_p) \to \mathbb{C}$ and every shift $s_0 \in \mathbb{C}$, there is $\sigma \in \mathbb{R}$ such that for all $s$ with $\operatorname{Re} s > \sigma$ the function $g \mapsto w(g)\,\Phi(g)\,\chi(\det g)\,|\det g|^{\,s+s_0}$ is $\mu_2$-integrable, where $|\cdot|$ is `modulus`, the scaling factor of multiplication on Haar measure.
--
--   This is the local absolute-convergence statement for the Godement–Jacquet zeta integral attached to a vector $w$ in the Whittaker model $V$ generated by $w_2^{\mathrm{base}}$ and a Schwartz–Bruhat function $\Phi$ on $2\times 2$ matrices, in the form allowing an arbitrary complex shift $s_0$ of the exponent. It is used to make the local zeta integrals and their coefficients at $p$ well defined in the Rankin–Selberg and converse-theorem parts of the Langlands–Tunnell argument.
